(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟩.\n$$" 13194139535661 true] [17592186359771 1113 #uuid "917351e8-3e93-5c8c-b787-a39fdea6cdc6" 13194139535661 true] [17592186359771 1145 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨1,0⟩,$ since the point $P(1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{0}}{{({e}^{0}+1)}^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{{({e}^{0}+1)}^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨1,0⟩+2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩+2⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩+⟨2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535661 true] [17592186359772 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359773 13194139535661 true] [17592186359772 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359774 13194139535661 true] [17592186359772 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359775 13194139535661 true] [17592186359772 10